sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant DEV as Connected device
    participant API as POST /iot/events
    participant IOT as IoTService
    participant DB as Database
    actor PH as Policyholder
    actor ADJ as Adjuster

    DEV->>API: {policy_number, source, kind, severity, readings}<br/>header X-Device-Key
    API->>API: constant-time key check, payload size limit
    API->>IOT: ingest(...)
    IOT->>DB: policy by number
    IOT->>IOT: event kind must match policy type<br/>(e.g. water_leak ↔ home)
    IOT->>DB: save IoTEvent

    alt open claim of same type within ±3 days
        IOT->>DB: event.claim = claim, add timeline entry
        IOT-->>ADJ: notification "new device evidence"
    else no matching claim
        IOT-->>PH: notification "incident detected, file a claim to attach it"
    end
    Note over IOT,PH: Notifications respect the holder's preferences (device alerts on/off)
    API-->>DEV: 201 {id, linked}

    PH->>API: GET /me/dashboard or /me/devices
    API->>DB: events in last 90 days
    API-->>PH: safety score = 100 − Σ penalty (high 8, medium 4, low 1)

    opt event not linked automatically
        PH->>API: POST /me/devices/{id}/attach {claim_id}
        API->>IOT: link(event, claim) after ownership + type checks
    end
